Web-888-local fix (no upstream equivalent): stop logging "socket error 2"
(mg_error, which also hard-closes) when epoll reports EPOLLERR for a
gracefully-closing peer. EPOLLERR fires on any pending error condition, but
also accompanies a normal peer close — the /admin websocket was being dropped
~0.5 s after connect with an mg_error log line every time the browser
navigated away or reconnected. Now SO_ERROR is read via getsockopt() first:
only a real pending socket error takes the mg_error path; a clean SO_ERROR
treats the event as readable/HUP so the normal read path closes the
connection quietly. Precedent: pkgs/sdrpp_server/sdrpp_server.cpp SO_ERROR
check. Scope: epoll branch only (the poll/select "socket error 3/4" paths
are not used by the Web-888 build and keep upstream behavior).
Background: docs/dev/mongoose-websocket-socket-error-investigation.md.

